"'''Just Can't Get Enough'''" is a song by American group [[Black Eyed Peas]], who also co-wrote it, along with Joshua Alvarez, Stephen Shadowen, [[Rodney Jerkins|Rodney "Darkchild" Jerkins]], and [[Julie Frost]], for the group's sixth studio album, ''[[The Beginning (Black Eyed Peas album)|The Beginning]]'' (2010). It was announced on January 21, 2011, as the album's second single and was released on February 8.

The song has been a success on the charts, reaching the top-five in many countries, such as New Zealand, Australia,<ref name="sc_Australia_The Black Eyed Peas"/> Greece, France,<ref name="sc_France_The Black Eyed Peas" /> United Kingdom and the United States,<ref name="US Hot 100">{{Cite magazine|url=http://www.billboard.com/articles/news/472182/katy-perrys-et-widens-lead-atop-hot-100|title=Katy Perry's 'E.T.' Widens Lead Atop Hot 100|date=April 6, 2011|first=Gary|last=Trust|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|publisher=[[Prometheus Global Media]]|access-date=April 6, 2011}}</ref> among others. The accompanying music video was filmed in Japan a week before the [[2011 Tōhoku earthquake and tsunami]].
As of June 2011, the single has sold more than 2,462,000 digital units in the US.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://music.yahoo.com/blogs/chart-watch/chart-watch-extra-top-20-songs-at-mid-year.html |title=Archived copy |access-date=April 12, 2012 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121006181241/http://music.yahoo.com/blogs/chart-watch/chart-watch-extra-top-20-songs-at-mid-year.html |archive-date=October 6, 2012 }}</ref>

