"Just Can't Get Enough" is a song by American group Black Eyed Peas, who also co-wrote it, along with Joshua Alvarez, Stephen Shadowen, Rodney "Darkchild" Jerkins, and Julie Frost, for the group's sixth studio album, The Beginning (2010). It was announced on January 21, 2011, as the album's second single and was released on February 8.

The song has been a success on the charts, reaching the top-five in many countries, such as New Zealand, Australia, Greece, France, United Kingdom and the United States, among others. The accompanying music video was filmed in Japan a week before the 2011 Tōhoku earthquake and tsunami.
As of June 2011, the single has sold more than 2,462,000 digital units in the US.

